  "notes": "Transcribed from the official Lincoln University 2026-2027 Academic Year Catalog. BS in Diagnostic Imaging: 45 units General Education + 16 units core + 34 units general ultrasound + 27 units concentrations/externships = 122 units. Term layout follows the catalog's published 'SUGGESTED COURSE SEQUENCING FOR THE BS IN DI DEGREE PROGRAM'. Concentration shown is Sonography (first-listed); the Echocardiography alternate is documented below and in the choice options. The catalog's suggested sequence sums to 115 units, not 122: it omits the 7 required concentration-elective units ('DI 234 or DI 235' 4 units + 'DI 244 or DI 245' 3 units for Sonography). Those two choice slots are placed here in Year 3 Fall and Year 3 Spring, the earliest prerequisite-satisfying positions (DI 234 requires DI 124; DI 235 requires DI 125; DI 244 requires DI 234; DI 245 requires DI 235); the catalog notes 'The order of major courses can be changed only with permissions of an advisor and the Program Director.' Year 4 Fall's 'Elective (General Education Course)' slot is ECON 10, the only required GE course not otherwise scheduled. The sequence lists 'ENG 82A Written Communications'; the course-description catalog lists ENG 82, shown as ENG 82A per the sequence. Externship codes are rendered 'DI 291A'/'DI 291B' (the sequence prints 'DI 291 A/B'). DI 210's prerequisite is 'Completion of all DI 100 series coursework' (satisfied by Year 2 Summer); DI 291A requires senior standing plus advisor/Program Director permission; DI 291B requires the last term of the program plus DI 291A/295A. Echocardiography alternate: Year 3 Fall DI 235, Year 3 Spring DI 245, Year 3 Summer DI 255, Year 4 Fall DI 265 + DI 295A, Year 4 Spring DI 295B; electives 'DI 231 or DI 234' (Year 3 Fall) and 'DI 241 or DI 244' (Year 3 Spring).",
